<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>method</key><string>app-store-connect</string>
  <key>destination</key><string>export</string>
  <key>signingStyle</key><string>manual</string>
  <key>teamID</key><string>DT93FSYJ9C</string>
  <key>signingCertificate</key><string>Apple Distribution</string>
  <!-- Pinned by UUID, NOT by name. Two installed profiles were once both named
       "Kya App Store" and one of them carried no com.apple.developer.applesignin
       entitlement, so selecting by name was ambiguous and could ship an app where
       Sign in with Apple cannot work. The App ID's Sign in with Apple capability
       was toggled off/on and a profile regenerated on 2026-09-16 while chasing
       an Apple-side sign-up failure; stale profiles are removed locally.

       Repinned 2026-09-21: enabling the Push Notifications capability invalidated
       the 2026-09-16 profile (it carried no aps-environment, so it could not sign
       a push build at all). Regenerated as "Kya App Store Push 2026-09-21" and
       verified by decoding it before use:
           aps-environment            = production
           com.apple.developer.applesignin = Default
       Both must be present. Sign in with Apple silently missing from the signed
       binary is what got build 4 rejected under guideline 2.1(a). -->
  <key>provisioningProfiles</key>
  <dict>
    <key>com.thekyaproject.app</key><string>9682294d-4253-4060-8fa4-2787f18b8b86</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
